    {
      "type": "row", "title": "Incident interpretation & telemetry coverage", "id": 105,
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 86 }, "collapsed": false
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "title": "How to read a production incident", "id": 29,
      "description": "Operator guide to the dashboard's health, workload, capacity, rollout, ingress, and scaling signals.",
      "datasource": { "type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 0, "y": 87 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "1. **Establish service health.** Gateway and edge scrapes should be healthy; worker scrape, golden-readiness, and release gates explain partial capacity.\n2. **Measure user impact.** Check create errors/rejections, wake failures, starting/stopping backlog, and ingress errors/latency.\n3. **Inspect workload state.** Running, hibernated, transient lifecycle, routes, and warm inventory show what the fleet is serving.\n4. **Check placement constraints.** Allocatable slots, per-worker memory admission, binding pools, and create concurrency identify the bottleneck.\n5. **Then inspect scaling.** Compare the provider MIG target with heartbeat-live workers and weighted demand. For scale-in, cordons must resolve as removed or aborted without deletion failures.\n6. **Protect rollout and billing durability.** Release mismatches gate placement; unflushed usage intervals must not persist.\n\nNomad schedules the worker system job, but **Nomad Autoscaler is retired**. The gateway alone writes the worker MIG size in both directions. GCE standby must remain **MANUAL** with zero suspended/stopped targets because its scale-out pool can power down a busy member."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "text", "title": "Telemetry semantics and remaining gaps", "id": 30,
      "datasource": { "type": "datasource", "uid": "grafana" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 10, "w": 12, "x": 12, "y": 87 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Gateway at 10s:** service health, sandbox inventory/routes, provider MIG target, weighted demand and queue, allocatable capacity, scaling/drain actions, create completions/rejections, and release gating.\n\n**Workers at 30s:** lifecycle states/counters, warm-pool behavior, memory and pool admission, create concurrency, usage durability/allocation counters, guest CPU recorded from closed intervals, readiness phases, process uptime, and release identity. **Edge:** replica health, traffic/errors, route/TLS outcomes, rate limits, bytes, wake latency, certificate lifetime, and raw leases.\n\n**Not emitted:** API create/exec/restore latency histograms, exec request/result counters, instantaneous host CPU, worker disk/network pressure, deploy annotations, or an explicit MIG-target poll failure counter. The MIG target series is absent until a provider poll succeeds; no-data is not zero. Benchmark latency remains offline evidence in `docs/benchmarks.md`."
      }
    },

    { "type": "row", "title": "Public ingress", "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 97 }, "id": 106, "collapsed": false },

    {
      "type": "stat", "title": "TLS certificate lifetime", "id": 31,
      "description": "Days until the earliest active edge certificate expires.",
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "sandbox-prom" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 6, "x": 0, "y": 98 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "d", "decimals": 1, "color": { "mode": "thresholds" }, "thresholds": { "steps": [ { "color": "red", "value": null }, { "color": "orange", "value": 3 }, { "color": "green", "value": 7 } ] } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": { "colorMode": "background", "graphMode": "none", "reduceOptions": { "calcs": ["lastNotNull"], "fields": "", "values": false } },
      "targets": [ { "refId": "A", "expr": "(min(sandbox_edge_certificate_expiry_timestamp_seconds{job=\"sandbox-edge\"}) - time()) / 86400" } ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries", "title": "Ingress connections and errors", "id": 32,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "sandbox-prom" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 9, "x": 6, "y": 98 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "fillOpacity": 10 } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom" }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" } },
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "sum(sandbox_edge_conns_open{job=\"sandbox-edge\"})", "legendFormat": "HTTPS open" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "sum(sandbox_edge_raw_conns_open{job=\"sandbox-edge\"})", "legendFormat": "raw open" },
        { "refId": "C", "expr": "sum(rate(sandbox_edge_conns_total{job=\"sandbox-edge\",result=\"error\"}[5m]))", "legendFormat": "HTTPS errors/s" },
        { "refId": "D", "expr": "sum(rate(sandbox_edge_raw_conns_total{job=\"sandbox-edge\",result=\"error\"}[5m]))", "legendFormat": "raw errors/s" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries", "title": "Wake latency (fleet quantiles)", "id": 33,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "sandbox-prom" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 9, "x": 15, "y": 98 },
      "fieldConfig": { "defaults": { "unit": "s", "custom": { "drawStyle": "line", "fillOpacity": 10 } }, "overrides": [] },
      "options": { "legend": { "displayMode": "list", "placement": "bottom" }, "tooltip": { "mode": "multi" } },
      "targets": [
        { "refId": "A", "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(sandbox_edge_wake_seconds_bucket{job=\"sandbox-edge\"}[5m])))", "legendFormat": "p50" },
        { "refId": "B", "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(sandbox_edge_wake_seconds_bucket{job=\"sandbox-edge\"}[5m])))", "legendFormat": "p95" },
        { "refId": "C", "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(sandbox_edge_wake_seconds_bucket{job=\"sandbox-edge\"}[5m])))", "legendFormat": "p99" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries", "title": "Raw lease pool", "id": 34,
      "datasource": { "type": "prometheus", "uid": "sandbox-prom" },
      "gridPos": { "h": 7, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 105 },
